=== WEB SOURCE → NATIVE MAPPING ===
  Web `ResponseViewer` is a presentational component (props: response, loading,
  history, onReplay; the only hook is `useTranslation`). It renders exactly three
  branches plus a history strip, and additionally EXPORTS a `SnippetPanel`:
    loading                  → Skeleton                       → TSSkeleton (shared feedback)
    !loading && !response    → EmptyState(noResponse)         → TSEmptyState (shared feedback)
    !loading && response     → FadeIn(status bar+body+headers) → TSFadeIn (shared motion)
    history.length>0         → RequestHistory GlassPanel       → TSGlassPanel (shared ui)
    export SnippetPanel      → cURL/JS/Python/Go + Copy        → public SnippetPanel view
  States: the web presentational source has loading / empty / content ONLY — the
  parent playground page owns the request lifecycle, so there is no query
  error/stale/offline branch in THIS surface (identical to sibling 0040 RequestBuilder).
  All three web states are reproduced; none are hidden (rule #2, #6-hidden-panels).
  Shared-component mapping (prompt "Shared components used"):
    @/components/ui       GlassPanel→TSGlassPanel, Button→Button(.plain)+tokens,
                          CopyButton→SnippetCopyButton (shared TSClipboard seam, labeled
                          Copy⇄Copied like the web `label`+`withToast`)
    @/components/feedback  Skeleton→TSSkeleton, EmptyState→TSEmptyState
    @/components/motion    FadeIn→TSFadeIn

